cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: KR-Housing-LongRAG-Bench
abstract: >-
  A copyright-safe Korean long-context benchmark for evaluating whether
  full-context LLMs can replace or complement RAG and table/tool pipelines over
  real housing announcements (입주자모집공고), public tabular data (MOLIT 실거래 /
  HUG 분양이력), and housing statutes. The public release contains QA labels,
  evidence locators, deterministic predicates, answerability labels, split and
  provider/region metadata, and long-context-bundle references — no raw source
  documents, no leaked answers, and no API keys. v0.9.3 keeps the 1,997 QA,
  questions and splits of v0.9 (dev 1,608 / test_public 389) and the v0.9.2
  gold fixes (342 evaluated test_public items). It fixes a closed-book locator
  leak (68 items whose locator revealed the answer; re-run) and a page-marker
  bug for Hangul page ids (dev recall under-counted; results unchanged),
  excludes 122 dev items whose gold page is not in their 512k bundle from the
  bundle settings, and adds human labels: 100 random dev items (7 errors,
  7.0%, Wilson 95% [3.4, 13.7]; excluded from evaluation), independent labels on the 80 judge-validation
  predictions, and the 74 Anthropic predictions on which six judges disagree.
  It adds verdicts for the re-runs, two Anthropic models and a four-judge
  panel. The v0.9.2 three-annotator test review (29 errors, 8.4%) and its gold
  fixes stand. The release is not leaderboard-ready and has no sealed hidden
  split.
type: dataset
version: v0.9.3
date-released: 2026-10-11
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/comsa33/kr-housing-longrag-bench"
